\n\n \n\nTherefore, $4∤7$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $7\\ne 4k.$" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420066 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1069 "q-221923" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1071 "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $3∣(14x+21y)$\n- $7∣(14x+21y)$\n- $4∣(14x+21y)$" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1072 #uuid "48fbd1ea-16f2-572a-98a1-c1983af51b24" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420071 1074 "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $14(1)+21(0)=14,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n14x+21y=7(2x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $2x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $7∣(14x+21y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $14(1)+21(0)=14,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420060 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1069 "q-221929" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1071 "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $2$ divides $(6x-18y)$\n- $3$ divides $(6x-18y)$\n- $5$ divides $(6x-18y)$" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1072 #uuid "63936aa1-e722-5014-a82a-6fe76f4b851d" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420072 1074 "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n6x-18y=2(3x-9y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $3x-9y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2$ divides $(6x-18y).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n6x-18y=3(2x-6y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $2x-6y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(6x-18y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=2$ and $y=1,$ we have $6(2)-18(1)=-6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420063 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420065 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420068 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420069 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1069 "q-221920" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1071 "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe notation $5∤6$ means {{field-1}}. It is equivalent to the statement that {{field-2}}{{field-3}} $k,$ we have {{field-4}}." 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1072 #uuid "8eb0e9a4-7a3a-5999-9897-bbedb74b2220" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420073 1074 "The notation $a∤b$ means $a$ does not divides $b.$ So, $5∤6$ means $5\\text{ doesn't divide }6.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb\\ne ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $5∤6$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $6\\ne 5k.$" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420074 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420078 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420074 1062 #uuid "56eb53ba-c780-5a71-a330-07b5e88ca9a3" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420074 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420071 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420075 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420077 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420075 1062 #uuid "6200d2fa-ec68-5795-8705-de7c6137e85c" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420075 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420070 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420076 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420075 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420076 1062 #uuid "8f90a01d-2bf3-5e73-ae54-8cf83cc03dfb" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420076 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162463 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420077 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420074 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420077 1062 #uuid "9fa38660-d8a3-5241-9915-730f9151df80" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420077 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420073 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420078 1062 #uuid "d7173f03-42ea-5a77-a52b-599bcf37ac02" 13194139534349 17592186045417 true] [17592186420078 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420072 13194139534349 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-3f8a0c05-783a-5bb8-ba35-0cfc1728bfdc" 17592186420027 "answer-0c6cecab-b539-59d3-83dc-06106b4873ed" 17592186420028 "answer-0e80c981-b97a-5513-91b8-2faa41d87131" 17592186420029 "answer-0ee48430-dc13-56f9-afff-d440154c4f60" 17592186420030 "answer-17d5b6db-f2d7-57e8-a2a5-1d92b46e0512" 17592186420031 "answer-1da65dc0-01b4-5b68-9fb5-2b24392ab3e7" 17592186420032 "answer-28361710-34ba-59ce-b434-53dba37859c0" 17592186420033 "answer-2faf54bf-f0f4-5f6a-ba0d-fb8c4f36a6dc" 17592186420034 "answer-4859316a-a30b-5139-b3a8-dda8a704ef63" 17592186420035 "answer-60887104-df4a-53c7-a034-7138745e6c35" 17592186420036 "answer-74adfba4-a612-51c0-b39d-230fa366846e" 17592186420037 "answer-75e38757